{{Codex|Art meets ingenuity with this beautifully deadly rifle.}}

The '''Tiberon Prime''' is the select-fire [[Prime]] version of the three round burst-fire rifle {{Weapon|Tiberon}}, featuring overall higher stats. Unique to the weapon is its three firing modes that can be swapped through its [[Alternate Fire]]: balanced statistics on its three round burst-fire mode, higher [[critical chance]] and [[critical multiplier]] on semi-auto mode, and higher [[status chance]] on full-auto mode. It was released alongside {{WF|Zephyr Prime}} and {{Weapon|Kronen Prime}}.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage by a small margin.
*Can use the Tiberon-exclusive {{M|Critical Precision}} mod.
*Can equip the Tiberon-exclusive {{M|Measured Burst}} mod ([[Conclave]] only).
*Three firing modes that can be cycled with [[Alternate Fire]]: 3-round burst, semi-auto, and full-auto.

{{Advantages|
*High accuracy.
*Very low [[recoil]], especially on Burst-fire and Semi-auto modes.
}}
{{Disadvantages|
*Burst-fire mode is linearly less efficient &ndash; sometimes a target may only die with four bullets, which requires an entire second burst to be fired, or a change to Fire Mode.
**This can also be mitigated by using quick melee with good timing, canceling the burst partway through.
*Full-auto mode has high recoil.
}}
{{WeaponComparison|Tiberon}}

==Acquisition==
{{PrimeTable}}
{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

===Vaultings===
*On [https://www.warframe.com/news/atlas-prime-access-ends-december-17 December 4th, 2019], it was announced that Tiberon Prime, alongside {{WF|Zephyr Prime}} and {{Weapon|Kronen Prime}}, would enter the [[Prime Vault]] and its relics retired from the drop tables on December 17th, 2019. Any preexisting components or fully-built weapons will remain as is.

==Trivia==
*Tiberon Prime is the first primary weapon to have three firing modes, namely burst-fire, semi-auto, and full-auto modes.
*Tiberon Prime is the second primary weapon with the ability to switch fire modes, the first being {{Weapon|Stradavar}}.

